              struct D {
                virtual int (*f() const noexcept)(int);
              };

            It was declared as 'int (*f() const)(int) noexcept' in the director class, which does
            not compile.

2026-10-31: wsfulton
            #2087 Fix a noexcept after the declarator of a function returning a function pointer or
            of a function pointer variable, which belongs to the function pointed to:

              int (*f())(int) noexcept;
              struct S {
