            reference using the wrong object, which could crash, given a class Klass, in:

              %shared_ptr(Klass)
              Klass *const &pointerreftest(Klass *const &k);

2026-10-31: wsfulton
            [C] Fix the C++ wrappers of a pointer to an enum passed or returned by const reference
            taking and returning a reference to the enum instead of the pointer, for example:

              enum E { A, B };
              void set(E *const &p);
