2026-10-31: wsfulton
            [R] Fix an R function passed for function pointer types that differ only in the
            qualifiers of their return type, such as 'char *(*)(int)' and 'const char *(*)(int)'.
            The value it returned was converted for whichever of the types was wrapped first. So a
            'char *' it returned could point into the R string instead of being a copy. C code
            changing that string then changed the R string. Each type now has its own conversion.

2026-10-31: wsfulton
            [R] Fix a parameter whose type is a typedef of a function pointer not taking an R
            function. Passing one gave an error such as "SWIG:TypeError in method 'apply',
            argument 2 of type 'FnPtr'" for:

              typedef int (*FnPtr)(int);
