2026-10-22: wsfulton
            [C] Add support for "argout" typemaps when wrapping C++ code. They were ignored, so their
            code, such as setting an output parameter, was missing from the wrappers. As for the other
            typemaps, an "argout" typemap that uses SWIG_exception or SWIG_fail needs the canthrow
            attribute. $result is the variable holding the return value, so an "argout" typemap that
            uses it for a function returning void is an error.

2026-10-22: wsfulton
            [C] Fix the $symname special variable, which was not expanded in some typemaps, such as a
            "check" typemap, giving a wrapper that did not compile. It is now expanded in all the
            typemaps used in a wrapper function.

            Also with the -namespace option, $symname no longer includes the namespace prefix, as in
            the other target languages. This changes $symname in typemaps, %exception and %exceptionvar
            for a class member, constructor or destructor and for the getter or setter of a variable.
            For example, with '-namespace ns', $symname is now 'Klass_method' instead of
            'ns_Klass_method' for the method 'method' of class 'Klass' and 'gvar_get' instead of
            'ns_gvar_get' for the getter of the global variable 'gvar'. It is unchanged for a function
            that is not a class member, such as 'func'.

