2026-10-22: wsfulton
            [Javascript] The code of an "in" typemap is no longer put inside an extra pair of braces,
            which no other target language adds. A local variable declared in the code of a typemap
            written with "" or %{ %} delimiters is now in the scope of the whole wrapper function, as
            in the other target languages, so it can clash with a variable of the same name declared
            by another typemap, for example when two parameters use this typemap:

              %typemap(in) int %{
                int tmp = 0;
                ...
                $1 = tmp;
              %}

            Such typemaps must be changed to use { } delimiters.

            *** POTENTIAL INCOMPATIBILITY ***

