2026-10-22: wsfulton
            [Lua] The array typemaps in typemaps.i are no longer supported and have been removed, for
            consistency with the other target languages. These are the INPUT, OUTPUT and INOUT
            typemaps for numbers, enums and pointers in a fixed size array, such as 'int INPUT[ANY]',
            or in an array passed with its length, such as '(double *INOUT, int)'. The helpers they
            used are removed too, so a typemap of your own that uses one no longer compiles. These are
            the functions SWIG_itable_size, SWIG_table_size, SWIG_read_<type>_num_array,
            SWIG_get_<type>_num_array_fixed, SWIG_get_<type>_num_array_var,
            SWIG_write_<type>_num_array, SWIG_read_ptr_array, SWIG_get_ptr_array_fixed,
            SWIG_get_ptr_array_var and SWIG_write_ptr_array, the macros SWIG_ALLOC_ARRAY,
            SWIG_FREE_ARRAY and SWIG_DECLARE_TYPEMAP_ARR_FN and the SWIG_TYPEMAP_NUM_ARR %define. To
            keep using them, copy them from typemaps.i in an earlier version of SWIG into an
            interface file.

            *** POTENTIAL INCOMPATIBILITY ***

