            [R] NULL and an empty vector, such as integer(0) or character(0), are now told apart,
            as the R wrappers no longer convert NULL to an empty vector before passing it to C/C++.
            NULL for a 'const std::vector<T> &' parameter now gives SWIG:NullReferenceError rather
            than an empty std::vector. NULL for a 'std::vector<T>' passed by value gives a SWIG
            TypeError. An empty vector is an empty std::vector, an array of zeros for a fixed size
            array and a pointer to no elements for a pointer to numbers. It gives a SWIG TypeError
            for a 'char *' string, a char array or a reference. A user scoercein typemap that
